# Accessibility (stack)

Generic a11y principles (semantics, keyboard, contrast, DOM order) live in `engineering/frontend`. Below is this stack's a11y wiring.

- Visible focus via Tailwind's `focus-visible:` variants (or the UI kit's focus ring) — don't replace it without an equivalent visible focus style.
- Toasts via an accessible toast/notification library with `aria-live` built in; don't hand-roll banners that miss it.
- Don't break the kit's a11y when overriding: keep `role`, `aria-*`, and keyboard handlers intact. A "styled" component that drops its semantics is a regression.
